9],["2026-08-17",154.01,670272]],"stock":{"a":3.9,"ad":"2026-08-17","atd":"2023-05-12","c":"agg and double","cl":154.01,"d":297,"fam":"2023-05","ft":"2023-05-12","g":1,"iid":"14046","ins":{"cd":"2026-07-29","cluster":"Auto / EV","co":"SURYODAY SMALL FIN BK LTD","has":true,"layer":"Bank - Small Finance Bank (deposit-funded lender; inclusive finance 44% of advances : secured retail + digital)","q":"Q1FY27","sec":"Small Finance Bank (microfinance-origin; JLG->individual-loan 'Vikas Loan' transition plus a secured retail build-out in used commercial vehicles and mortgages)","st":[{"status":"Unthemed","subtheme":"General – Small Finance Bank (microfinance-origin; JLG->individual-loan 'Vikas Loan' transition plus a secured retail build-out in used commercial vehicles and mortgages)","tag":"General","theme":"Auto & Mobility","tier":""}],"thesis":"Suryoday's Q1 FY27 is the quarter the CGFMU insurance thesis actually paid out in cash: **₹387cr of claims received in the quarter** (₹386cr in the opening remarks) took net NPA to ₹170cr / 1.2%, and management pulled the full-year ROA target forward — the 1.6% that was guided for *Q4* FY27 was already printed in *Q1*. Underneath, the mix is shifting fast — inclusive-finance share of advances fell 48%→44%, individual loans are ~80% of monthly onboarding, and the CLOU (credit-line-on-UPI, Paytm) book is compounding 5-10% month-on-month — while gross advances grew 32.5% YoY to ₹14,376cr against deposits +29.4% to ₹14,634cr. The catch is that the print is flattered by a one-off: **~₹46cr of PSLC income from ₹1,600cr of certificates sold**, which the CFO says drops to ₹10-15cr per quarter for the next two quarters, so Q2 is guided to be \"a little subdued\" even as the ₹300cr+ FY27 PAT guidance is held.","trig":[]},"lm":"2026-07","m":1637,"mem":0,"pdd":"2024-04-18","prev_stage":null,"prev_zone_vpe":null,"r":20.6,"s":"SURYODAY","sig":"","sx":{"SMA_50":"173.4","base_count":"","drawdown_from_prev_signal":"","duration_from_prev_signal":""